{"id":9092710,"docketId":66358972,"caseName":"Rondon v. Indiana","caseNameFull":"Rondon v. Indiana Hinton v. Alabama Martin v. Alabama Ellis v. Lynaugh, Director, Texas Department of Corrections","slug":"rondon-v-indiana","docketNumber":"No. 89-5593; No. 89-5595; No. 89-5626; No. 89-5683","dateFiled":"1989-11-13","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1989,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":0,"judges":"Brennan, Marshall","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":9086907,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1244,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<p id=\"Av9c\"><page-number citation-index=\"1\" label=\"969\">*969</page-number>Sup. Ct. Ind.;</p>\n<p id=\"A7iV\">Sup. Ct. Ala.;</p>\n<docketnumber id=\"Ak75\"><page-number citation-index=\"1\" label=\"970\">*970</page-number>No. 89-5626.</docketnumber>\n<docketnumber id=\"AdI5\">No. 89-5683.</docketnumber>\n<p id=\"AqlqC\">Sup. Ct. Ala.; and</p>\n<p id=\"ADEi\">C. A. 5th Cir. Certiorari denied. Reported below: No. 89-5593, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9711264\"><a href=\"/opinion/2074021/rondon-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Rondon v. State\">534 N. E. 2d 719</a></span>; No. 89-5595, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1738169\"><a href=\"/opinion/1738169/ex-parte-hinton/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex Parte Hinton\">548 So. 2d 562</a></span>; No. 89-5626, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9936604\"><a href=\"/opinion/1738198/ex-parte-martin/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex Parte Martin\">548 So. 2d 496</a></span>; No. 89-5683, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9478959\"><a href=\"/opinion/522207/edward-anthony-ellis-v-james-a-lynaugh-director-texas-department-of/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Edward Anthony Ellis v. James A. Lynaugh, Director, Texas...\">873 F. 2d 830</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9086908,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":595,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b908-6\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"ABKK\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b908-7\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}